From ac8d61a04c2997f76511e807b4938aeb9444c23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "erik.hauan" <erik.hauan@radiantvs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:55:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] node-scanner, noderec: slot capacity, jit_load and
 observed-at behind S1/S4

Behaviour: the scanner carries per-engine slot capacity (SlotsByEngine),
jit_load flags (JITLoadByEngine) and the models-observed heartbeat
(ModelsObservedAt) on each DirectoryNode. A successful /v1/models fetch
records them; a transient miss restores the last recorded values; forget
drops them; dropSelf migrates them to the new host UUID.

Seams used: S1 (noderec.DirectoryNode embeds LocalNodeExt, defined in
services/shared/noderec/local_ext.go; wire keys unchanged), S4 (daemon field
local *localScanState plus one-line nil-safe hooks record/cached/migrate/
forget; bodies in services/nvpair-node-scanner/local_capacity.go).

Proving tests: TestS1_Nil, TestLocalNodeExtJSONKeys (shared ./noderec/);
TestS4_Nil, TestLocalEnrichSetsSlotsAndObservedAt,
TestLocalEnrichFallbackRestoresSlots, TestLocalForgetAndDropSelfSlotCaches,
TestRefreshSlotChangeReportsChange, TestApplyModelsObservedAtHeartbeat
(nvpair-node-scanner).

Feature-group commit for catch-up step 2, exported as
local/patches/001-scanner-slot-capacity.patch. It touches only upstream files
and new files so it replays onto NVIDIA; fork-test fallout and records follow
in the next commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
